@startuml Callback Flow
skinparam style strictuml

actor Browser
participant "Gateway\n/auth/callback" as GW
database Redis
participant Keycloak

Browser -> GW: GET /api/v1/auth/callback?code=...&state=...
activate GW

== Validate State ==

GW -> Redis: GetDel(state)
Redis --> GW: return_to = "/game"

note right of GW: State is single-use\n(atomic read + delete)

== Exchange Code for Tokens ==

GW -> Keycloak: POST /token\ngrant_type=authorization_code\ncode, redirect_uri, client_id, client_secret
activate Keycloak
Keycloak --> GW: access_token, id_token,\nrefresh_token, expires_in
deactivate Keycloak

== Parse Claims ==

GW -> GW: ParseUnverifiedClaims(access_token)\n→ user_id, username, email, roles

== kc_action Flow (optional) ==

alt kc_action_status present (password/email change)
    GW -> Redis: Get(existing_session_id from cookie)
    Redis --> GW: existing session
    GW -> GW: Update tokens in session
    GW -> Redis: Update(session_id, updated_session)
    Browser <-- GW: 302 Redirect → return_to
else Normal login/register
end

== Create Session ==

GW -> GW: Build SessionData\n{access_token, id_token, refresh_token,\nuser_id, username, email, roles, expires_at}

GW -> Redis: Create(session_data, TTL=refresh_expires_in)
Redis --> GW: session_id (UUID)

== Set Cookie & Redirect ==

GW -> GW: Set-Cookie: gordle_session=session_id\nHttpOnly, Path=/

Browser <-- GW: 302 Redirect → "/game"\n+ Set-Cookie header
deactivate GW

@enduml
